    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "12410aa5_05dc5888",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnCaps.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 235,
      "author": {
        "id": 7953
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-26T15:59:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`getDepthAttachmentDimensions()` is called just before allocating depth buffer, it is unlikely be called without a initialized texture. Or we can change this method arg from `TextureProxy*` to `graphite::Texture*`?",
      "parentUuid": "aa0f40e7_7c018766",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 234,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 235,
        "endChar": 91
      },
      "revId": "c0aa7b3e0b11fdfb9e9bfde74ae1737d55b6996a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "50219eca_d4ddcf1a",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnCaps.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 235,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-28T20:26:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was less worried about whether it would be initialized or not. I was more wondering if in the future (with BackendTextureViews) we\u0027ll be storing the full textures format as well as the planes (or just the full and Skia infers the plane\u0027s format itself). So in that world we would already have all the format info we needed. So I was suggesting do we just do that now and store on the DawnTextureInfo both formats. Then we don\u0027t need to pass in a TextureProxy or Texture into this call but just a TextureInfo.\n\nIf we decide to keep this closer to how you have it, I think I would say lets pass in a Texture* instead of a TextureProxy*",
      "parentUuid": "12410aa5_05dc5888",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 234,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 235,
        "endChar": 91
      },
      "revId": "c0aa7b3e0b11fdfb9e9bfde74ae1737d55b6996a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b8411648_849a803d",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnCaps.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 235,
      "author": {
        "id": 7953
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-28T22:30:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not familiar with `BackendTextureViews` work. I think fixing the meeting issue is urgent. I feel it is better to have a simple fix first, we can change it when `BackendTextureViews` is ready.\n\nI tried using `Texture*` instead of `TextureProxy*`, but `Texture*` doesn\u0027t contain aspect info. We have to either use `TextureProxy*` or add an `aspect` param. And right now, the aspect is dawn specified thing. We don\u0027t have aspect defined in skia level, right?",
      "parentUuid": "50219eca_d4ddcf1a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 234,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 235,
        "endChar": 91
      },
      "revId": "c0aa7b3e0b11fdfb9e9bfde74ae1737d55b6996a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "11fcc311_8ae79f0c",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnCaps.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 235,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-29T15:47:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t have to do anything specific with `BackendTextureViews` now. I was just mentioning them as my motivation for my suggested change. To be more clear, we would land something like, https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/820297. Then update all the Chrome callers that make YUV images to also give us the full yuv format (this is something we\u0027ll have to do eventually down the road anyways). Then your helper function here can just be:\n\n`getDepthAttachmentDimensions(const TextureInfo\u0026, size_t dimensions)`.\n\nFWIW as a side note the aspect in dawn lives on the DawnTextureInfo/Spec which you can also get off of the Texture as well as the TextureProxy.",
      "parentUuid": "b8411648_849a803d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 234,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 235,
        "endChar": 91
      },
      "revId": "c0aa7b3e0b11fdfb9e9bfde74ae1737d55b6996a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
